"'''Ayo Technology'''" is the fourth single from [[50 Cent]]'s third album, ''[[Curtis (50 Cent album)|Curtis]]'' (2007).<ref>Dave (June 29, 2007). [http://www.rapbasement.com/content/view/3018/35/ 50s next single "She Wants It" featuring Justin Timberlake] {{webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070701125153/http://www.rapbasement.com/content/view/3018/35/ |date=July 1, 2007 }}. Rap Basement. Retrieved July 21, 2007.</ref><ref>[http://www.50cent.com/0CFFCFFFF0002D51F001600028450/Content/ContentDetail.aspx "Ayo Technology" Video Premiere!!] {{webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071006221533/http://www.50cent.com/0CFFCFFFF0002D51F001600028450/Content/ContentDetail.aspx |date=October 6, 2007 }}. 50cent.com. Retrieved August 2, 2007.</ref><ref>Omar Burgess (July 5, 2007). [http://www.hiphopdx.com/index/news/id.5426/title.did-interscope-shut-down-50s-youtube-hustle Did Interscope Shut Down 50's YouTube Hustle?]. HipHopDX. Retrieved July 21, 2007.</ref> It was released on July 24, 2007. The song, featuring [[Justin Timberlake]] and vocals from [[Timbaland]], who also produced the song along with [[Danja (record producer)|Danja]], has peaked at number five on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]]. Internationally, the song peaked within the top ten of the charts in many countries, including [[Australia]], [[Denmark]] and the [[United Kingdom]]. The song has since been covered by [[Milow]], a Belgian singer-songwriter whose version was successful in a number of countries, including Belgium, Spain, Germany, Italy, and the Netherlands. The song was also covered by Greek-Belgian singer [[Katerine Avgoustakis]].

